#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:22
msgid "Adding an inset to the figure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:24
msgid ""
"To plot an inset figure inside another larger figure, we can use the :meth:"
"`pygmt.Figure.inset` method. After a large figure has been created, call "
"``inset`` using a ``with`` statement, and new plot elements will be added to "
"the inset figure instead of the larger figure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:31
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis, Box, Position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:39
msgid ""
"Prior to creating an inset figure, a larger figure must first be plotted. In "
"the example below, :meth:`pygmt.Figure.coast` is used to create a map of the "
"US state of Massachusetts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:45
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=[-74, -69.5, 41, 43],  # Set bounding box of the large figure\n"
"    borders=\"2/thin\",  # Plot state boundaries with thin lines\n"
"    shorelines=\"thin\",  # Plot coastline with thin lines\n"
"    projection=\"M15c\",  # Set Mercator projection and size of 15 "
"centimeter\n"
"    land=\"lightyellow\",  # Color land areas light yellow\n"
"    water=\"lightblue\",  # Color water areas light blue\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True),  # Set frame with annotations\n"
")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:63
msgid ""
"The :meth:`pygmt.Figure.inset` method uses a context manager, and is called "
"using a ``with`` statement. The ``position`` parameter, including the inset "
"width, is required to plot the inset. In the example below, the inset is "
"placed at the Bottom Left (``BL``) inside the plot. The ``box`` parameter "
"can set the fill and border of the inset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:71
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=[-74, -69.5, 41, 43],\n"
"    borders=\"2/thin\",\n"
"    shorelines=\"thin\",\n"
"    projection=\"M15c\",\n"
"    land=\"lightyellow\",\n"
"    water=\"lightblue\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True),\n"
")\n"
"with fig.inset(position=Position(\"BL\"), width=3, box=Box(pen=\"black\", "
"fill=\"lightred\")):\n"
"    # pass is used to exit the with statement as no plotting methods are "
"called\n"
"    pass\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:91
msgid ""
"When placed at the Bottom Left corner inside the plot, the default location "
"is in contact with the nearby axis or axes. The offsets along the x- and y-"
"axes can be set with the ``offset`` parameter of the ``Position`` class. If "
"only one offset is passed, it is applied to both axes. Each offset can have "
"its own unit. In the example below, the inset is shifted 0.5 centimeters on "
"the x-axis and 0.2 centimeters on the y-axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:99
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=[-74, -69.5, 41, 43],\n"
"    borders=\"2/thin\",\n"
"    shorelines=\"thin\",\n"
"    projection=\"M15c\",\n"
"    land=\"lightyellow\",\n"
"    water=\"lightblue\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True),\n"
")\n"
"with fig.inset(\n"
"    position=Position(\"BL\", offset=(0.5, 0.2)),\n"
"    width=3,\n"
"    box=Box(pen=\"black\", fill=\"lightred\"),\n"
"):\n"
"    pass\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:123
msgid ""
"Standard plotting methods can be called from within the ``inset`` context "
"manager. The example below uses :meth:`pygmt.Figure.coast` to plot a zoomed "
"out map that selectively paints the state of Massachusetts to show its "
"location relative to other states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/advanced/insets.rst:130
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=[-74, -69.5, 41, 43],\n"
"    borders=\"2/thin\",\n"
"    shorelines=\"thin\",\n"
"    projection=\"M15c\",\n"
"    land=\"lightyellow\",\n"
"    water=\"lightblue\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True),\n"
")\n"
"# This does not include an inset fill as it is covered by the inset figure. "
"Inset\n"
"# width/height are determined by the ``region`` and ``projection`` "
"parameters.\n"
"with fig.inset(\n"
"    position=Position(\"BL\", offset=(0.5, 0.2)),\n"
"    box=Box(pen=\"black\"),\n"
"    region=[-80, -65, 35, 50],\n"
"    projection=\"M3c\",\n"
"):\n"
"    # Use a plotting method to create a figure inside the inset.\n"
"    fig.coast(\n"
"        land=\"gray\",\n"
"        borders=[1, 2],\n"
"        shorelines=\"1/thin\",\n"
"        water=\"white\",\n"
"        dcw=\"US.MA+gred\",  # Use dcw to selectively highlight an area\n"
"    )\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

